    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:2",
      "cellIndex": 2,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "> **Reference**\n>- Section 6.3 \"Damped Harmonic Motion\". Jerry B. Marion. Classical Dynamics of particles and systems. Academic Press.\n",
      "sourceSha256": "2829abdd80959925c559c0d4e1e937a762acbf0670274e0028660f4b243e61d3",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:3",
      "cellIndex": 3,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Damping force proportional to velocity",
      "sourceSha256": "54501766383fa005764cb20a0ffbf7dcc359a9332dbdbbbc65e7a5d6509c7d9c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:4",
      "cellIndex": 4,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "![shabana_fig_1_11.png]([embedded image omitted])",
      "sourceSha256": "17fbd1cc2bf97a11357d110bb2178318ebb183f2e219632cf66b9a14ceaa5f81",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:5",
      "cellIndex": 5,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "A force $\\vec{F}(t)$ is exerted upon a system with the following characteristics:\n\n- m : mass\n- c : damping coefficient for a force proportional to velocity\n- k : spring constant following Hooke's law $F_\\mathrm{spring} = - k x$",
      "sourceSha256": "55699f4d5d06abe2d79d840fa6f1b585f042bea2c235839907c9f3206d82ad16",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\vec{F}(t)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "F_\\mathrm{spring} = - k x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:6",
      "cellIndex": 6,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "import sympy as sm # import functions for symbolic manipulations\nfrom sympy.physics import mechanics as me\nme.init_vprinting() # dot notation for velocity and acceleration\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")",
      "sourceSha256": "1e498d2c45c426292100b8937934bc62aeeeb140bfbf97e75fd242de1154367d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [
          "sympy",
          "sympy.physics",
          "warnings"
        ],
        "calls": [
          "me.init_vprinting",
          "warnings.filterwarnings"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:7",
      "cellIndex": 7,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "t = sm.symbols('t') # time\nm, k, c = sm.symbols('m, k, c', positive = True)\nx, F = me.dynamicsymbols('x F')\nN = sm.physics.vector.ReferenceFrame('N') # frame of reference N using cartesian coordinates\nr_m = x* N.x\n\noneHalf = sm.Rational(1,2) # we can use 0.5 \nv_m = r_m.diff(t,N)\nT = oneHalf* m* v_m.dot(v_m)\n\nV = oneHalf* k* r_m.dot(r_m)\n\nL = sm.Eq(sm.Symbol('\\mathcal{L}'), T - V).simplify()\nL",
      "sourceSha256": "3096f0e850fa25eaecaf7d66f74073d703cb396ee5e948346646512e778508da",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "                   2      2\n                k⋅x    m⋅ẋ \n\\mathcal{L} = - ──── + ────\n                 2      2  ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\mathcal{L} = - \\frac{k x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{m \\dot{x}^{2}}{2}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "me.dynamicsymbols",
          "r_m.diff",
          "r_m.dot",
          "simplify",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.Rational",
          "sm.Symbol",
          "sm.physics.vector.ReferenceFrame",
          "sm.symbols",
          "v_m.dot"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:8",
      "cellIndex": 8,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The nonconservative forces exerted upon the system.",
      "sourceSha256": "acd8cb54445cc36eedba1b41f26512b8d3c43f9e969d8a470acd5ba1ed707045",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:9",
      "cellIndex": 9,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "![shabana_fig_1_11b.png]([embedded image omitted])",
      "sourceSha256": "22beebfe9c72f25a9e68862369dbfdbb5347c11727c48ae862a1dd452d7ef03e",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:10",
      "cellIndex": 10,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "f = F* N.x - c* r_m.diff(t,N)\nf",
      "sourceSha256": "280ed1ed5d736d37a20c41877d0c398158754614f399034c53422f026781a1b4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "(-c⋅ẋ + F) n_x",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle (- c \\dot{x} + F)\\mathbf{\\hat{n}_x}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "r_m.diff"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:11",
      "cellIndex": 11,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Given that the generalized coordinate used is the vector component, its corresponding generalized force is the resultant of forces ($\\delta W = f \\delta x = Q_x \\delta x$).",
      "sourceSha256": "8be262ad2812743d48f732ee1befb96b56835b8f48d004465b4246039d89e405",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\delta W = f \\delta x = Q_x \\delta x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:12",
      "cellIndex": 12,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_Q_symbol = sm.Symbol('Q_x')\nx_Q = f.dot(N.x)\nsm.Eq(x_Q_symbol, x_Q)",
      "sourceSha256": "372d9db06c2c3ef44fc2cef6f65a703eb8481afecb8c0e70dcf42d77b81afd8d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "Qₓ = -c⋅ẋ + F",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle Q_{x} = - c \\dot{x} + F$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "f.dot",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.Symbol"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:13",
      "cellIndex": 13,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We usually write the Euler-Lagrange equation with generalized forces as\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d} t} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial \\dot{q_i}} \\mathcal{L} \n- \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial q_i} \\mathcal{L} = Q_i ,\n$$\nin this case is",
      "sourceSha256": "02c1852667472ac78e1792a7e3d97359fab82acf16a3b03d1c2e1af87136aa50",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d} t} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial \\dot{q_i}} \\mathcal{L} \n- \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial q_i} \\mathcal{L} = Q_i ,\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:14",
      "cellIndex": 14,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_dtdqp = L.rhs.diff(x.diff(t) ).diff(t)\nx_dq = L.rhs.diff(x)\nx_EL_noForces = x_dtdqp - x_dq\nx_EL = sm.Eq(x_EL_noForces.simplify(), x_Q)\nx_EL",
      "sourceSha256": "b7a3d179713f63956f71d73488a3227eda9d528cef90aab7406fc86fc938292e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "k⋅x + m⋅ẍ = -c⋅ẋ + F",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle k x + m \\ddot{x} = - c \\dot{x} + F$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "L.rhs.diff",
          "diff",
          "sm.Eq",
          "x.diff",
          "x_EL_noForces.simplify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:15",
      "cellIndex": 15,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "For the analysis of oscillations, the equation of dynamics is usually written leaving the forcing force aside.",
      "sourceSha256": "e48a8d41260b812b0d29ee57fe7da2fa1412c4000e151e33cb312da86dcb7cbb",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:16",
      "cellIndex": 16,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_noForcing = sm.solve(x_EL, F)[0] \nsm.Eq( x_EL_noForcing, F) ",
      "sourceSha256": "6b74fdee339cad3dfd03755a8e1c46b92f92954845a6bd093f0bffd1bb70e310",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "c⋅ẋ + k⋅x + m⋅ẍ = F",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle c \\dot{x} + k x + m \\ddot{x} = F$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.solve"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:17",
      "cellIndex": 17,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Rotations\n\nIt must not be forgotten that the generalized coordinate can be an angle $\\theta$ and in that case the corresponding Euler-Lagrange equation is\n$$\n\\Gamma \\dot{\\theta} + \\kappa \\theta + I \\ddot{\\theta} = \\tau,\n$$\nwhere the coefficients are\n- $\\Gamma$ : rotational friction\n- $\\kappa$ : torsional stiffness\n- $I$ : moment of inertia\n- $\\tau$ : torque (the generalized force that corresponds to $\\theta$)",
      "sourceSha256": "d7f637209fbfaf9b99a8b4b2c40d327dd9ee7df03c2254423623fd102b68eb15",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\theta"
        },
        {
          "kind": "display",
          "latex": "\n\\Gamma \\dot{\\theta} + \\kappa \\theta + I \\ddot{\\theta} = \\tau,\n"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\Gamma"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\kappa"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "I"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\tau"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\theta"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:18",
      "cellIndex": 18,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Dynamics without external forcing",
      "sourceSha256": "6be1c6b7e146530234b2c2b3fb026f204b9e122fc1b2fb3f46ee1d7db82534b8",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:19",
      "cellIndex": 19,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "![shabana_fig_1_11_recorte.png]([embedded image omitted])",
      "sourceSha256": "104c9e9cda07a42cf2d653172b49a81ba1e349fc66215ab010e2e84612cff7ee",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:20",
      "cellIndex": 20,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "If there is no external force ($F = 0$), the previous linear differential equation is homogeneous.",
      "sourceSha256": "8878f4c126c45429d018087e147534351238fff2d8d7e819da9c5bb94b7cb3e7",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "F = 0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:21",
      "cellIndex": 21,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_homogeneous =  x_EL_noForcing.subs(F,0)\nsm.Eq(x_EL_homogeneous, 0)",
      "sourceSha256": "400faef72e00ddb987552964968e420b8fdfdb6031e28cdfa01d5a2b3d11bc32",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "c⋅ẋ + k⋅x + m⋅ẍ = 0",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle c \\dot{x} + k x + m \\ddot{x} = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.Eq",
          "x_EL_noForcing.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:22",
      "cellIndex": 22,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "We usually divide by the mass, ",
      "sourceSha256": "fdd70ef4c7005e6e430c666ca6afe5f3b585bf42c6fcdd92d18fd596adefd7f9",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:23",
      "cellIndex": 23,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_mass = (x_EL_homogeneous/ m).expand()\nsm.Eq(x_EL_mass, 0)",
      "sourceSha256": "d21ed1e4cb34a3c87ced8276b9aa933bbb5874d6c731cda640af360b5c9ca6a7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "c⋅ẋ   k⋅x        \n─── + ─── + ẍ = 0\n m     m         ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{c \\dot{x}}{m} + \\frac{k x}{m} + \\ddot{x} = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "expand",
          "sm.Eq"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:24",
      "cellIndex": 24,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "to assign particular symbols to the coefficients of $x$ and $\\dot{x}$:\n- natural frequency of oscillation of the system: $\\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m} }$,\n- damping ratio (or damping rate): $\\zeta = \\frac{c}{C_c}$, where $C_c = 2 \\sqrt{k m} = 2 m \\omega$ is the critical damping coefficient.",
      "sourceSha256": "70726af56643bd74f9f2bae97713c2cd5dccfea2e49e4998db075740060ee9e1",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\dot{x}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\omega = \\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m} }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\zeta = \\frac{c}{C_c}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_c = 2 \\sqrt{k m} = 2 m \\omega"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:25",
      "cellIndex": 25,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "omega, zeta = sm.symbols('omega zeta', real = True)\nx_EL_ing = x_EL_mass.subs([(k/m, omega**2), (c/m, 2* zeta* omega) ]).simplify()\nsm.Eq((x_EL_ing).expand(), 0)",
      "sourceSha256": "49bc10aa559b8c50704fca8bc64e123f02450fdf48fd4992f4e8e79511e90638",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": " 2                    \nω ⋅x + 2⋅ω⋅ζ⋅ẋ + ẍ = 0",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\omega^{2} x + 2 \\omega \\zeta \\dot{x} + \\ddot{x} = 0$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "simplify",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.symbols",
          "x_EL_ing.expand",
          "x_EL_mass.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:26",
      "cellIndex": 26,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The solution using complex exponential functions",
      "sourceSha256": "daac73bc46e9713a02c8c454af504a401c955999b91db54887068d430b2fd088",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:27",
      "cellIndex": 27,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_EL_ing_sol = sm.dsolve(x_EL_ing)\nx_EL_ing_sol.simplify()",
      "sourceSha256": "31100a37d5cd900016c8cc999634cb553cede43276b8033fcb1d04439876c33a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "    ⎛           ________               ________⎞        \n    ⎜          ╱  2                   ╱  2     ⎟        \n    ⎜    ω⋅t⋅╲╱  ζ  - 1        -ω⋅t⋅╲╱  ζ  - 1 ⎟  -ω⋅t⋅ζ\nx = ⎝C₁⋅ℯ                + C₂⋅ℯ                ⎠⋅ℯ      ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = \\left(C_{1} e^{\\omega t \\sqrt{\\zeta^{2} - 1}} + C_{2} e^{- \\omega t \\sqrt{\\zeta^{2} - 1}}\\right) e^{- \\omega t \\zeta}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.dsolve",
          "x_EL_ing_sol.simplify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:28",
      "cellIndex": 28,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "is a linear combination of the two possible solutions, with coefficients $C_i$.",
      "sourceSha256": "74dfd622683f78cdda2a583137da7b14f789d7774e69efa793d725a9b89a7f5d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_i"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:29",
      "cellIndex": 29,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Relaxation period $\\tau$\nRegardless of the behavior that $x(t)$ presents as a function of $\\zeta$, the term $\\operatorname{e}^{- \\omega \\zeta t}$ is responsible for reducing the amplitude as $t$ increases.\nIn fact, each time this **relaxation period** $\\tau = \\frac{1}{\\omega \\zeta}$ elapses, the amplitude decays by $\\operatorname{e}^{-1}$.\nIt is considered that after $\\sim 10 \\tau$ the oscillation is considered extinct.",
      "sourceSha256": "2e3f174cd2128680afb34d3fc0b07b981ffa95008089115db19e5b123430782d",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\tau"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x(t)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\zeta"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\operatorname{e}^{- \\omega \\zeta t}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "t"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\tau = \\frac{1}{\\omega \\zeta}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\operatorname{e}^{-1}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\sim 10 \\tau"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:30",
      "cellIndex": 30,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Critically damped, $\\zeta = 1$\nIf $\\zeta = 1$ the simplest behavior is achieved.",
      "sourceSha256": "b9da23e4ec91836cd83ce735db8dbea2bf156c4a66139ed9b3f9f167045d9971",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\zeta = 1"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\zeta = 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:31",
      "cellIndex": 31,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_crit = x_EL_ing_sol.subs(zeta,1).simplify()\nx_crit",
      "sourceSha256": "693a017768c7e9e46603aaee3c4d27dccb0322683c7fb1dfa5544dccd8af0e74",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "               -ω⋅t\nx = (C₁ + C₂)⋅ℯ    ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = \\left(C_{1} + C_{2}\\right) e^{- \\omega t}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "simplify",
          "x_EL_ing_sol.subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:32",
      "cellIndex": 32,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "which is an exponential decay toward the equilibrium position.",
      "sourceSha256": "94e2a326a057ed7d48c109cac2cdbbf795bc7ce3ac7e471bc30fb96699afedd9",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:33",
      "cellIndex": 33,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "To visualize these behaviors, the $C_i$ can be determined as a function of the known $x$ and $\\dot{x}$ at a given $t$, the so-called initial conditions.\nIf for $t_0 = 0$ we know $x_0 = x(t_0)$ and $\\dot{x}_0 = \\dot{x}(t_0)$",
      "sourceSha256": "c5dc5a32e6e7822c5a47595404a3d777910140b72235b07240aac104d2a07df5",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_i"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\dot{x}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "t"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "t_0 = 0"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "x_0 = x(t_0)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "\\dot{x}_0 = \\dot{x}(t_0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:34",
      "cellIndex": 34,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_0, dx_0 = sm.symbols('x_0 \\dot{x}_0', real=True)\ncrit_condInit = [sm.Eq(x_0, x_crit.args[1].subs(t, 0) ), sm.Eq(dx_0, x_crit.args[1].diff(t).subs(t, 0) ) ]\ncrit_condInit",
      "sourceSha256": "23ca658c0da6f0aa89da479b75474e709e0d35728ac2a975622854d9d31a4f45",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "[x₀ = C₁ + C₂, \\dot{x}₀ = -ω⋅(C₁ + C₂)]",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ x_{0} = C_{1} + C_{2}, \\  \\dot{x}_0 = - \\omega \\left(C_{1} + C_{2}\\right)\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "diff",
          "sm.Eq",
          "sm.symbols",
          "subs"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:35",
      "cellIndex": 35,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "where we can solve for $C_i$ ",
      "sourceSha256": "160e01bff2dbec7fe3b16079e4f7f097036ffd3b014205221b53095e9e734b0c",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": [
        {
          "kind": "inline",
          "latex": "C_i"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:36",
      "cellIndex": 36,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "crit_condInit_sol = sm.solve(crit_condInit)\ncrit_condInit_sol",
      "sourceSha256": "11d4b3928c3c202ac1bf23d550e26a7f11150724872706e76a156587e645dece",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "[{C₁: -C₂ + x₀, \\dot{x}₀: -ω⋅x₀}]",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle \\left[ \\left\\{ C_{1} : - C_{2} + x_{0}, \\  \\dot{x}_0 : - \\omega x_{0}\\right\\}\\right]$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "sm.solve"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:37",
      "cellIndex": 37,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "x_crit_condInit = x_crit.subs(crit_condInit_sol[0] )\nx_crit_condInit.simplify()",
      "sourceSha256": "b7e5ca4b7fcddb04536f420f55e8b387ae6585517cf3074f9ca9b7bf7596ac77",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "        -ω⋅t\nx = x₀⋅ℯ    ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = x_{0} e^{- \\omega t}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
        "imports": [],
        "calls": [
          "x_crit.subs",
          "x_crit_condInit.simplify"
        ],
        "literalAssignments": {},
        "parseError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:38",
      "cellIndex": 38,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "For example, if we assign",
      "sourceSha256": "0a6572a054e6941975877d1ff3a00cc2d41d4374e2306c4bc9b6b352f92ffbed",
      "outputs": [],
      "outputMimeTypes": [],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "math": []
    },
    {
      "sourceRef": "index:39",
      "cellIndex": 39,
      "originalCellId": null,
      "type": "code",
      "source": "k = 100 # [N m-1]\nm = 1 # [kg]\nx_0_magnitude = 1 # [m]\ndx_0_magnitude = -100 # [m s-1]\n\nparameters ={\n    x_0 : x_0_magnitude,\n    dx_0 : dx_0_magnitude,\n    omega : sm.sqrt(k/m)\n}\nx_crit_parameters = x_crit_condInit.subs(parameters)\nx_crit_parameters",
      "sourceSha256": "c6efd85eb4c31602d00dac78f4500eea1d6cd86862110e5492f49550b1220321",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "execute_result",
          "text/plain": "     -10.0⋅t\nx = ℯ       ",
          "text/latex": "$\\displaystyle x = e^{- 10.0 t}$"
        }
      ],
      "outputMimeTypes": [
        "image/png",
        "text/latex",
        "text/plain"
      ],
      "attachmentNames": [],
      "pythonAst": {
